thanked you

253
00:12:15,967 --> 00:12:18,200
for saving me from Liza.

254
00:12:19,200 --> 00:12:20,167
So thank you, okay?

255
00:12:20,300 --> 00:12:21,533
I mean...

256
00:12:21,667 --> 00:12:23,833
Joahae, Jin Ho.

257
00:12:25,200 --> 00:12:29,767
[ROMANTIC MUSIC PLAYING]

258
00:12:29,900 --> 00:12:31,767
Yeah, you're welcome.

259
00:12:31,900 --> 00:12:35,433
[ROMANTIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

260
00:12:37,367 --> 00:12:38,933
Let's eat, come on.

261
00:12:39,067 --> 00:12:40,967
Ah... This is really good, huh.

262
00:12:41,100 --> 00:12:44,533
[ROMANTIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

263
00:12:58,333 --> 00:12:59,433
Coffee?

264
00:12:59,567 --> 00:13:01,000
No, thanks.

265
00:13:02,467 --> 00:13:04,033
[SIGHS IN RELIEF]

266
00:13:07,333 --> 00:13:09,167
It's beautiful here, right?

267
00:13:09,300 --> 00:13:11,333
You never get tired
of looking at it.

268
00:13:14,500 --> 00:13:15,767
I know.

269
00:13:15,900 --> 00:13:19,967
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

270
00:13:23,333 --> 00:13:26,433
You know, you should've just
stayed here after you left.

271
00:13:26,567 --> 00:13:29,333
Then maybe you wouldn't have
gone back to Liza.

272
00:13:32,500 --> 00:13:36,167
I know you two have history,
but you get it.

273
00:13:36,300 --> 00:13:37,400
Of course,

274
00:13:37,533 --> 00:13:40,333
your life here would've been
much more peaceful, right?

275
00:13:42,833 --> 00:13:44,533
You're right, Joey.

276
00:13:46,800 --> 00:13:48,667
I wanna apologize.

277
00:13:52,033 --> 00:13:54,567
I really used you before

278
00:13:54,700 --> 00:13:57,133
just to find Theresa.

279
00:13:57,300 --> 00:13:59,300
That's Liza's real name.

280
00:14:00,933 --> 00:14:02,567
And...

281
00:14:03,500 --> 00:14:06,133
I'm not a real agent, Joey.

282
00:14:07,267 --> 00:14:11,100
I was with a bad group
back in Korea.

283
00:14:12,233 --> 00:14:13,833
Theresa and I...

284
00:14:15,100 --> 00:14:16,767
We were together.

285
00:14:16,900 --> 00:14:18,333
We had a plan.

286
00:14:18,467 --> 00:14:19,767
Own enough money,

287
00:14:19,900 --> 00:14:23,300
then disappear somewhere quiet
and start over.

288
00:14:24,167 --> 00:14:25,500
But...

289
00:14:26,667 --> 00:14:28,700
She had bigger dreams.

290
00:14:31,233 --> 00:14:34,100
Let me guess,
for her drug empire?

291
00:14:35,233 --> 00:14:36,700
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC PLAYING]

292
00:14:36,833 --> 00:14:38,533
Unbelievable.

293
00:14:38,667 --> 00:14:43,200
Even I struggle just handling
my social media pages.

294
00:14:45,033 --> 00:14:46,900
When I found out again,

295
00:14:47,800 --> 00:14:50,167
I thought I could remind her

296
00:14:50,300 --> 00:14:53,833
of the peaceful life we wanted,

297
00:14:53,967 --> 00:14:57,800
but, she's not
that person anymore.

298
00:14:59,033 --> 00:15:02,533
She is really ambitious.

299
00:15:04,567 --> 00:15:05,533
Well...

300
00:15:05,667 --> 00:15:08,000
there's nothing wrong
with being ambitious.

301
00:15:08,133 --> 00:15:10,400
The problem is, the kind
of ambition she chose

302
00:15:10,533 --> 00:15:14,000
destroys families and ruins
people's lives.

303
00:15:15,233 --> 00:15:16,867
And to be honest...

304
00:15:18,100 --> 00:15:20,900
You know, being with you guys,

305
00:15:21,033 --> 00:15:24,267
laughing, arguing,

306
00:15:24,400 --> 00:15:26,367
protecting each other,

307
00:15:27,533 --> 00:15:30,033
I think that's the life
I want now.

308
00:15:32,567 --> 00:15:34,800
That life really suits you
better anyway,

309
00:15:34,967 --> 00:15:37,533
being a saviour and a protector.

310
00:15:38,133 --> 00:15:39,667
Really?

311
00:15:40,300 --> 00:15:41,933
Mmm-hmm.

312
00:15:42,367 --> 00:15:43,133
I can't even count

313
00:15:43,267 --> 00:15:45,633
how many times you've saved me
already.

314
00:15:46,867 --> 00:15:49,200
The bottom line is,
you always choose

315
00:15:49,333 --> 00:15:51,400
to do what's right

316
00:15:51,533 --> 00:15:53,533
because you're a good person.

317
00:15:54,800 --> 00:15:57,300
You're a good person, Jin Ho.

318
00:15:57,433 --> 00:16:01,400
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

319
00:16:09,533 --> 00:16:11,833
Hurry up already!
We're starting at 12 noon!

320
00:16:11,967 --> 00:16:13,300
Guys, fix the seating already!

321
00:16:13,433 --> 00:16:15,233
Oh, hello!
Yes, welcome!

322
00:16:15,367 --> 00:16:17,133
Quick, quick!

323
00:16:17,267 --> 00:16:19,233
Hurry up!

324
00:16:19,367 --> 00:16:22,467
Hurry!
Fix the chairs!

325
00:16:22,600 --> 00:16:23,900
Excuse me.

326
00:16:24,467 --> 00:16:26,667
Are you Eun Ji?

327
00:16:27,600 --> 00:16:29,067
Ah, I know you!

328
00:16:29,200 --> 00:16:30,200
Yeah.

329
00:16:30,333 --> 00:16:31,267
Weren't we the ones
who defended you

330
00:16:31,400 --> 00:16:32,833
from the people
you owed money to?

331
00:16:32,967 --> 00:16:34,900
<i>- You're running away from us?
- Sir!</i>

332
00:16:35,033 --> 00:16:35,900
<i> Please help me!</i>

333
00:16:36,033 --> 00:16:37,767
<i>This person owes us
a lot of money.</i>

334
00:16:38,433 --> 00:16:39,933
[THUDS]

335
00:16:40,067 --> 00:16:41,500
- Maybe that's Eman Pacquiao.
- [INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

336
00:16:41,667 --> 00:16:42,667
Eman Pacquiao?

337
00:16:42,800 --> 00:16:44,267
You said before that since
we saved you,

338
00:16:44,400 --> 00:16:46,567
you wouldn't lie to us.

339
00:16:47,233 --> 00:16:50,267
Okay, we're here because we're
looking for Jin Ho.

340
00:16:50,867 --> 00:16:52,267
Do you know where he is?

341
00:16:52,400 --> 00:16:54,667
I don't know.
I do not see him.

342
00:16:54,800 --> 00:16:55,867
Sorry, sorry.

343
00:16:56,000 --> 00:16:58,667
But you know where he might've
gone, right?

344
00:16:58,800 --> 00:17:00,533
No, I don't know.
Sorry, sorry.

345
00:17:00,667 --> 00:17:02,067
Ah, no, no Tagalog.

346
00:17:02,200 --> 00:17:03,133
Only little English, okay?

347
00:17:03,267 --> 00:17:04,600
Busy, busy! Sorry, sorry!

348
00:17:04,733 --> 00:17:06,100
Bye!

349
00:17:06,233 --> 00:17:08,133
[SHOUTS IN KOREAN]

350
00:17:08,267 --> 00:17:09,700
That punk.

351
00:17:09,833 --> 00:17:12,567
Before, he used to speak Tagalog
so fluently.

352
00:17:13,600 --> 00:17:15,567
I'm sure he knows where Jin Ho
is.

353
00:17:16,267 --> 00:17:18,800
But he definitely won't talk.

354
00:17:24,433 --> 00:17:25,600
[SIGHS IN RELIEF]

355
00:17:25,733 --> 00:17:28,133
[SPEAKING IN KOREAN]

356
00:17:28,633 --> 00:17:30,167
What did you say?

357
00:17:31,033 --> 00:17:32,567
- Nothing.
- Ah.

358
00:17:33,467 --> 00:17:35,967
I know you want to go home
already.

359
00:17:36,100 --> 00:17:39,167
I was just, ah,
letting a little time pass.

360
00:17:41,933 --> 00:17:44,600
Just make sure it's safe,

361
00:17:44,733 --> 00:17:46,933
and I will take you back
to your family.

362
00:17:47,067 --> 00:17:48,100
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

363
00:17:48,267 --> 00:17:49,433
Really?

364
00:17:50,633 --> 00:17:52,200
Thank you, Jin Ho.

365
00:17:53,633 --> 00:17:56,033
I just need to take care
of few things first.

366
00:17:56,167 --> 00:17:57,333
Okay?

367
00:17:57,467 --> 00:18:01,567
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

368
00:18:07,100 --> 00:18:10,767
[PHONE KEYS CLICKING]

369
00:18:10,900 --> 00:18:12,400
[RINGING]

370
00:18:12,533 --> 00:18:13,333
Hurry up, hurry up.

371
00:18:13,467 --> 00:18:14,667
Get the things from the car.

372
00:18:14,800 --> 00:18:16,200
Our guests are waiting.

373
00:18:16,333 --> 00:18:17,733
[PHONE RINGS]

374
00:18:18,733 --> 00:18:19,767
[SPEAKS IN KOREAN]

375
00:18:19,900 --> 00:18:20,833
Jin Ho?

376
00:18:20,967 --> 00:18:22,333
Eun Ji...

377
00:18:22,500 --> 00:18:26,767
[SPEAKING IN KOREAN]

378
00:18:28,100 --> 00:18:31,200
[SPEAKING IN KOREAN]

379
00:18:31,333 --> 00:18:34,300
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

380
00:18:35,533 --> 00:18:37,133
[SIGHS]

381
00:18:39,133 --> 00:18:42,000
[SPEAKING IN KOREAN]

382
00:18:42,567 --> 00:18:47,033
[SPEAKING IN KOREAN]

383
00:18:47,167 --> 00:18:51,167
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

384
00:19:02,367 --> 00:19:06,467
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

385
00:19:10,333 --> 00:19:11,967
[ENGINE STARTS]

386
00:19:13,233 --> 00:19:16,167
[REVVING]

387
00:19:16,300 --> 00:19:19,967
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

388
00:19:23,500 --> 00:19:24,700
Come on, hurry up, hurry up!

389
00:19:24,833 --> 00:19:26,200
[CAR CHIMES]

390
00:19:29,300 --> 00:19:30,767
[ENGINE STARTS]

391
00:19:32,567 --> 00:19:35,200
[REVVING]

392
00:19:35,533 --> 00:19:37,000
It's been 2 days already,
Miguel.

393
00:19:38,467 --> 00:19:41,133
We should've found Joey by now.

394
00:19:41,267 --> 00:19:43,733
We'll find her.

395
00:19:43,867 --> 00:19:45,800
I'll bring Joey back here.

396
00:19:47,933 --> 00:19:50,100
And we'll return this to her.

397
00:19:51,867 --> 00:19:54,167
[PHONE RINGING]

398
00:19:54,300 --> 00:19:56,867
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

399
00:19:57,000 --> 00:19:58,600
Hello, Peter?

400
00:19:58,733 --> 00:20:00,500
Uncle...

401
00:20:00,633 --> 00:20:03,100
Uncle, we're following Jin Ho's
friend right now.

402
00:20:03,267 --> 00:20:04,967
- Friend?
- Yes, a friend.

403
00:20:05,100 --> 00:20:07,000
<i> His business partner.</i>

404
00:20:07,133 --> 00:20:09,767
Looks like he's the one who'll
lead us to Jin Ho.

405
00:20:09,900 --> 00:20:10,867
Where are you?

406
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:12,433
I'll follow.

407
00:20:14,400 --> 00:20:16,900
<i>In Sta. Monica,
at the small town there.</i>

408
00:20:17,667 --> 00:20:19,567
Copy, we're on our way.

409
00:20:25,267 --> 00:20:27,033
[GUN COCKS]

410
00:20:27,167 --> 00:20:29,033
We are switching vehicles

411
00:20:29,167 --> 00:20:31,267
because the police and media,

412
00:20:31,400 --> 00:20:33,700
they are probably looking
for my car.

413
00:20:33,833 --> 00:20:35,800
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

414
00:20:35,967 --> 00:20:38,433
And once I drop you off
at your house,

415
00:20:38,567 --> 00:20:40,800
I have to leave immediately.

416
00:20:41,233 --> 00:20:42,333
Right away?

417
00:20:42,467 --> 00:20:43,867
Why?

418
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:47,400
Because your father
might arrest me.

419
00:20:47,533 --> 00:20:49,433
No, he won't do that.

420
00:20:49,567 --> 00:20:52,100
I'll talk to him.
I'll explain everything to him.

421
00:20:52,233 --> 00:20:54,267
I'll fix all of this.

422
00:20:54,400 --> 00:20:56,167
That's a promise, Jin Ho.

423
00:20:58,467 --> 00:20:59,133
[SIGHS]

424
00:20:59,267 --> 00:21:01,533
[SPEAKS IN KOREAN]

425
00:21:01,667 --> 00:21:02,733
Huh?

426
00:21:02,867 --> 00:21:05,200
- What was that?
- [PHONE RINGING]

427
00:21:06,600 --> 00:21:07,900
Hello?

428
00:21:08,033 --> 00:21:09,400
Eun Ji?

429
00:21:10,967 --> 00:21:12,500
- Okay.
- [STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

430
00:21:13,100 --> 00:21:14,967
He's here.
Let's go.

431
00:21:15,100 --> 00:21:18,133
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

432
00:21:18,867 --> 00:21:24,167
[PHONE RINGING]

433
00:21:26,067 --> 00:21:29,633
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

434
00:21:32,467 --> 00:21:34,100
This better be good.

435
00:21:34,233 --> 00:21:36,233
We already know the location.

436
00:21:36,367 --> 00:21:38,667
We're heading there now to
capture Jin Ho

437
00:21:38,800 --> 00:21:41,533
and the beloved daughter
of Miguel Delgado.

438
00:21:41,700 --> 00:21:42,900
Good.

439
00:21:43,033 --> 00:21:44,333
<i>You know, I realized something.</i>

440
00:21:44,467 --> 00:21:46,733
We'll finally silence Jin Ho,

441
00:21:46,867 --> 00:21:48,867
and at the same time,
get revenge on that Delgado

442
00:21:49,000 --> 00:21:50,267
through her beloved daughter.

443
00:21:50,400 --> 00:21:52,433
Two birds with one stone.

444
00:21:52,567 --> 00:21:54,700
That's efficient revenge, Liza.

445
00:21:55,567 --> 00:21:58,933
Now finish them off.

446
00:21:59,067 --> 00:22:03,033
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

447
00:22:09,600 --> 00:22:13,633
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

448
00:22:15,300 --> 00:22:16,433
They're about to escape.

449
00:22:16,567 --> 00:22:18,067
Finish them off, Matias!

450
00:22:18,200 --> 00:22:19,433
- Hide!
- [POLICE SIREN WAILING]

451
00:22:19,567 --> 00:22:21,200
Kang Dae-Hyun,
you're under arrest!

452
00:22:21,333 --> 00:22:22,733
I'll fix all of this.

453
00:22:22,867 --> 00:22:24,533
That person should
never be trusted!

454
00:22:24,667 --> 00:22:25,500
What were you thinking?

455
00:22:25,633 --> 00:22:27,400
When I say I'll get revenge,

456
00:22:27,533 --> 00:22:29,167
- I'll get revenge!
- [GUN FIRING]

457
00:22:29,300 --> 00:22:33,000
I won't stop until that cursed
syndicate is gone,

458
00:22:33,133 --> 00:22:34,967
especially their leader,
Berdugo.

459
00:22:35,100 --> 00:22:37,133
If I were the leader of that
syndicate,

460
00:22:37,267 --> 00:22:39,600
I probably would've had you
killed too!
